{"kind":"report","text":"READY-FOR-REVIEW at exact head 7a260ce94dc988590fcb0fd0c6cacc486fdfdd3c on branch task/world-basis, artifact git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:65dfe52eef293d32e8dfcbcac08d13a2df6f8929.\n\nAgainst the conditions of the request. The convention is decided and ratified rather than settled in passing: proposal a47da8f3a28d0ae8ae92d06c9b357368b20533ed, ratified by hugh at d188bee146075d4dd7afe2cfdbbf7812ccc06d22. A statement describing behaviour rests on the artifacts for that behaviour, and whoever changes behaviour supersedes the prior artifact for the same path. The projector surfaces describes-a-superseded-world distinctly from ordinary staleness, and marks artifacts with an empty rests_on as unable to flare. SKILL.md discipline 8 and the AGENTS.md loop are updated to match what landed. The alternative the request allowed — recording that this class of invalidation stays a human vigilance duty — was not taken.\n\nGates actually run on that exact head: go vet clean, the full go test suite passing, gofmt clean for every file this branch touches. Seven tests, each verified mutation-sensitive by breaking the implementation and confirming a named test fails. One early probe reported a clean pass because the mutation broke compilation rather than behaviour; it was re-run in a form that compiles, and it fails as it should.\n\nThe second commit exists because I measured before anyone reviewed. On the real log the succession mark fired on 55 of 88 artifacts across 9 distinct paths, since one unrecorded succession repeats on every later link of a path chain. The per-artifact fact is true and stays in the projection; the human summary now names both numbers. I judged a mark that trains readers to scroll past it worse than no mark. The evidence is recorded at 64838014af89003ff83bdba28bcbc3acba61089c, and whether the repair is the right one is a fair thing for the review to disagree with.\n\nTwo limits stated rather than closed: exact string path comparison, which this change is itself a case of, and reference documentation that does not yet describe the marks, which belongs to the documentation set request. One pre-existing gofmt miss in spike/internal/nexus is untouched.\n\nNot merged. The merge artifact will supersede the prior artifact for the path, which is the first exercise of the convention on itself.","body":{"branch":"task/world-basis","head":"7a260ce94dc988590fcb0fd0c6cacc486fdfdd3c"}}